# Inert803 generic Finance dependency admission prototype

SOURCE ONLY. No production caller, adapter, registry, URL, migration, native fixture, provider or DB run. No full803/private-closure acceptance. Trusted internal DB classification purpose and snapshot-time authorization contract still require integration approval.

Primitive apps/documents/template_finance_admission.py uses fixed SQL identifiers and internally supplied exact binding/run/version/template/document/kind/run-case/tenant/synthetic tuples. Separate targeted document/source closure MUST authorize those tuples first. No inferred same-case relation replaces that proof. Fresh observer identity, default connection/raw connection and RR entry token bind every phase. Generic documents calls recipient_access with observer.pk, not publication recipients.

Engineering bounds:100 binding work items per entry (not just100 runs),100 distinct runs,256KiB canonicalDBUTF8JSONB snapshot,1000inputs,1MiB aggregate snapshot bytes. Ledger shared across primitive instances within the entry. This is a Finance dependency ledger; composition with other domain admission ledgers and whole-operation accounting remains unimplemented. No RSS/database-work/through-commit revocation guarantee.

Nonstatement runs never query/classify/transfer snapshot. Statements admit size before array count and count before expansion; guarded structural checks return internal boolean only. Missing/null/malformed structures hold, including malformed tail after a PPE match: explicitly stricter than native short-circuit for malformed history. Ordinary statements gain no new PPE grant requirement. PPE statements call native readable before snapshot transfer; unchanged recipient_access remains afterward. No arbitrary interphase callbacks or writes. Identity and canonical SHA256/size/count/discriminator rechecked around loading/native helper, and loaded classification checked against native predicate. RR alone does not prevent same-connection mutation; this is a trusted straight-line read-only sequence, not a sandbox for arbitrary hooks.

Snapshot remains necessary for native helper; no hidden source predicate is weakened. Fixed hold messages return no classification/content. No public result besides None. Grants and native Case relation access remain native. No model immutability claimed.

Eight pure tests normal/-O pass: classification valid/malformed truth table, item and binding bounds, SQL phase ordering, grant-before-payload, postload agreement and shared context/ledger structure, nonstatement branch, no writes/top-level Finance imports. These tests do NOT execute Finance helpers or SQL and do NOT prove native equivalence. No DB tests executed or defined with fabricated runs. Legitimate Finance constructor scope remains unproven: known statement fixture setup invokes analysis pipeline, and inspection stopped before potentially held dependencies. Native SQL syntax/table compatibility, canonical byte boundaries, real grants, mutation/concurrency behavior and integrated fixture equivalence are UNRUN. Keep this module inert pending independent review and permitted fixture proof.

Review hardening: row() rejects unknown SQL and nonpositive/noninteger PK before any query; fixed internal payload SQL joins the closed allowlist. New statement runs reserve aggregate bytes immediately after size admission, before count/classification. A later shape failure leaves a conservative unusable reservation (no refund/retry bypass). A previously statement-stamped run entering the nonstatement branch holds. Ten pure normal/-O checks include executable fake-scalar aggregate-denial and retained-charge contrasts; no Finance helper or DB execution. Cross-domain operation ledger composition remains a separate unimplemented plan.
